From 972d8ce74ab1ebb383119691543c964add3fcf2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:35:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: the live resync sweep spares a link
 whose child card's links changed during the rebuild

Held.links bounds the task_links sweep by key (parent>child), so a key that
was unlinked (acked by a concurrent reconcile before the links snapshot) and
linked again (acked after it) still counted as "in the file when the rebuild
began": the sweep deleted and tombstoned it while the Board held it.

link_tasks / unlink_tasks write a linked / unlinked event on the child card,
so a link is now a sweep candidate only while its child has no such event at
or after `since`. The check is part of the candidate SQL, so it is re-checked
inside the apply transaction too.

held_at_start now reads each child table's outbox cards with grouped IN reads
instead of one SELECT per op (review nit).

Test: test_a_link_unlinked_and_relinked_mid_rebuild_is_not_swept (the
reviewer's probe) is RED on d5285da514 and GREEN here; 14/14 in the file.

